# Forensic Investigation Progress & Checklist

## Incident Overview
- Host: ssh-prod-01 (CentOS 7 Linux)
- Primary Incident Type: SSH Root Brute Force, Monero Cryptomining, Multi-stage Persistence, Anti-Forensics (Log Wiping)
- Status: Investigation & Remediation Planning Complete

## Timeline of Events (UTC)
1. 2026-08-15 00:53:24 - 00:54:52: External SSH brute-force attack against root user initiated from attacker origin IP `/disk/var/log/secure:141`.
2. 2026-08-15 00:54:55: Attacker successfully authenticates as root via SSH password brute force `/disk/var/log/secure:178`.
3. 2026-08-15 00:55 - 01:29: Attacker conducts post-exploitation activity:
   - Dropped and executed Monero cryptominer binary at `/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg` (`/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`, `/sas/alerts.json`).
   - Installed cron persistence in `/var/spool/cron/root` (`/disk/var/spool/cron/root:5`, `/sas/alerts.json`).
   - Installed shell-init persistence in `/root/.bashrc` (`/disk/root/.bashrc:2`).
   - Installed systemd service persistence at `/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service` (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service`, `/sas/alerts.json`).
   - Planted NOPASSWD sudo backdoor in `/etc/sudoers.d/devops` (`/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops:3`).
   - Cleared authentication logs causing log gap between 00:54:55 and 01:29:12 (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin`, `/disk/var/log/secure:178`).
   - Executed hydra brute-force tool against internal targets from devops user account context (`/disk/home/devops/.bash_history:6`).
4. 2026-08-15 03:20: Incident detected and intake logged by SOC (`/sas/handoff/intake.pdf`).


==> /app/intrusion-report.md <==
# Post-Compromise Forensic Intrusion Report

## Executive Summary
Host `ssh-prod-01` (CentOS 7 Linux) suffered a multi-stage compromise initiated via external SSH root credential brute-forcing. The attacker successfully authenticated as `root`, deployed an XMRig Monero cryptominer, established multi-layered persistence across four distinct mechanisms (cron, systemd service, shell init, and a sudoers backdoor), cleared system authentication logs to evade detection, and conducted internal reconnaissance/pivoting via `hydra` against internal targets.

## Attacker Entities and Indicators of Compromise (IoCs)
- **Origin Attacker IP:** `198.51.100.78` (`/disk/var/log/secure:178`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`)
