## Comprehensive Attack Chain Analysis

### 1. Initial Access & Credential Access
The attacker initiated a high-frequency SSH password brute-force campaign against host `ssh-prod-01` targeting common accounts (`oracle`, `test`, `admin`, `postgres`, `root`) from source IP `198.51.100.78` (`/disk/var/log/secure:141`). At 2026-08-15 00:54:55 UTC, the attacker successfully authenticated as user `root` due to weak root credentials and permissive SSH baseline configurations (`/disk/var/log/secure:178`, `/disk/etc/ssh/sshd_config`).

