# Comprehensive Post-Incident Remediation & Containment Plan

## Executive Summary
This remediation plan outlines prioritized, step-by-step procedures to contain the active breach on `ssh-prod-01`, eradicate all persistence mechanisms, harden host baselines, and reconcile the draft change ticket CHG-3182. In accordance with forensic best practices, all actions prioritize backup and quarantine over destructive deletion.

---

## Reconciled Change Ticket CHG-3182

Below is the updated and corrected change ticket reconciled against forensic evidence in `/disk` and `/sas`:

| # | Action | Target | Status | Note / Rationale & Evidence |
|---|--------|--------|--------|-----------------------------|
| 1 | Block source IP inbound | `198.51.100.78` | PROPOSED | **RECONCILED**: Corrected attacker IP from stale `203.0.113.9` to `198.51.100.78` (`/disk/var/log/secure:178`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`). |
| 2 | Patch CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep) | RDP | REJECTED | **RECONCILED**: Rejected BlueKeep patch claim. Host is CentOS Linux; entry was SSH brute force (`/disk/etc/os-release`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`). |
| 3 | Remove cron miner | `/var/spool/cron/root` | OPEN | **RECONCILED**: Downgraded from DONE to OPEN. Cron persistent beacon on line 5 requires quarantine and removal (`/disk/var/spool/cron/root:5`). |
| 4 | Remove shell-init persistence | `/root/.bashrc` | TODO | **ADDED**: Quarantine and remove `PROMPT_COMMAND` beacon on line 2 (`/disk/root/.bashrc:2`). |
| 5 | Remove systemd persistence | `/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service` | TODO | **ADDED**: Disable, stop, and quarantine helper service (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service`). |
| 6 | Remove sudoers backdoor | `/etc/sudoers.d/devops` | TODO | **ADDED**: Remove NOPASSWD ALL backdoor entry (`/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops:3`). |
| 7 | Kill miner process & quarantine binary | `/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg` | TODO | **ADDED**: Terminate process PID 1337 and quarantine binary sample (`/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`). |
